# --- OpenOCD (dbt debug) helpers. Not for the J-Link server: they call
# --- procedures defined in scripts/debug/openocd/rza1l.cfg.

# Load the RAM-linked image and leave the core at its entry point, ready to
# `continue`. Same steps as tools/deluge_jlink.py: halt without pulling nRESET,
# MMU/caches off, VBAR, DMA stopped, load, SVC mode with IRQ/FIQ masked.
# `dbt gdb` sets $deluge_elf and $deluge_entry, which selects the AHB-AP load
# (about 2.5x faster); otherwise this falls back to GDB's own `load`.
define deluge-load
  if $_isvoid($deluge_elf)
    monitor deluge_prepare
    maintenance flush register-cache
    load
    set $cpsr = 0x1DF
  else
    # The load runs inside one `monitor` command (about 20 s through a
    # GD32/STM32F103 DAPLink); without a longer timeout GDB drops the reply.
    set remotetimeout 120
    eval "monitor deluge_load %s 0x%x", $deluge_elf, $deluge_entry
    set remotetimeout 2
    maintenance flush register-cache
  end
end
document deluge-load
Halt-only reset, prepare the RZ/A1L and load the current ELF into RAM (OpenOCD only).
Then `continue` to run it. RTT: tools/openocd_rtt.py <elf> in another terminal.
